@* Card page breadcrumb — card.md Layout block #0, Interactions §5.1: "Browse / {SetName} / {CardTitle}".
   Browse is live (/browse) and the crumb links straight there. The set crumb stays an inert
   "future link" span -- not because Set pages are deferred (they're live at /set/{id} too),
   but because CardIdentity doesn't carry the set id this crumb would need to link to it
   (owner ruling: present-but-disabled with an honest tooltip, never a dead link). The leaf
   crumb is plain --ink text, not a link (card.md §5.1 item 5). *@
<div class="breadcrumb">
    <a class="crumb-link" href="browse">Browse</a>
    <span class="crumb-sep">›</span>
    <span class="crumb-link" title="@SetTooltip">@SetName</span>
    <span class="crumb-sep">›</span>
    <span class="crumb-leaf">@CardTitle</span>
</div>

@code {
    // Reusable single source of truth for this tooltip string — Task 16 renders the
    // identity-header subline's deferred set segment and must show byte-identical copy
    // rather than a re-typed duplicate literal.
    public const string SetTooltip = "Set link arrives in a later phase";

    [Parameter]
    public string SetName { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter]
    public string CardTitle { get; set; } = "";
}
